Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.570
Speaker 1: Let's try Luke from Indiana.

00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:02.570
Luke from Indiana.

00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:03.570
Please save us.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.029
Luke, I can hear you sort of what's going
on?

00:00:05.029 --> 00:00:06.029
Yeah.

00:00:06.029 --> 00:00:07.540
Speaker 2: Well, how's it going, it's going
well.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:18.340
Basically, what I want to talk about is a
lot of people that don't live in rural areas

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:21.000
don't understand truly how deep the urban
rural divide is.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Yeah.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.090
With the vaccinations, we've been hanging
out about 40 percent in Indiana for weeks

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:28.090
now, right.

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:30.130
And it's just not going up.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:34.539
Speaker 1: Yeah, you know, I actually went
to Indiana a couple of years ago and I was

00:00:34.539 --> 00:00:35.649
in rural northern Indiana.

00:00:35.649 --> 00:00:37.039
So it was like Goshen.

00:00:37.039 --> 00:00:41.199
Speaker 2: And I really I'm about I'm about
an hour west that I'm in Valparaiso.

00:00:41.199 --> 00:00:42.239
Speaker 1: OK, yeah.

00:00:42.239 --> 00:00:47.710
It was like Goshen and Shipshewana and all
these little little places and spending some

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:48.710
time there.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:57.309
I like of course, all those people voted for
Trump.

00:00:57.309 --> 00:00:59.469
You drive around, all you see is Amish folks
shooting ranges and evangelical churches.

00:00:59.469 --> 00:01:05.540
If that's what you grow up around and you're
not exposed to different types of people,

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:06.780
you're not exposed to.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:10.750
Hey, there's a whole alternative view here
of empiricism and science.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:20.040
Of course, abortion and guns are the most
important issues.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:26.170
And of course, you voted for Donald Trump,
even if half the stuff he says isn't even

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:28.790
is isn't isn't is not even true and sincere.

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:32.860
So, yeah, I think that a lot of people who
just spend their time in cities, they don't

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:36.950
get how it gets to this point in the rural
parts of the country.

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:44.610
And I think it would be useful for people
to spend some time there and better understand

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:46.920
how it happens, as you're pointing out.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:48.840
Speaker 2: Oh, yeah.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:02:02.020
And I think a lot of the problem, too, is
a lot of the people here, like you said, they

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:03.600
grew up in that scenario.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:04.600
Yeah.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:12.930
And they don't feel like anyone's trying to
reach out and change their mind at all, like.

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:13.930
Right.

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:18.849
I live in one of the more outside of Indianapolis.

00:02:18.849 --> 00:02:26.030
It's one of the more liberal places in Indiana
because we have a steel mill about.

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:56.310
Forty minutes away, that's one of the biggest
employers in the area, right, but even that

00:02:56.310 --> 00:03:22.760
a lot of those people voted for Trump just
because they don't think that any of the Democrats

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:32.079
are doing anything to reach out to them, they
feel pretty alienated.

00:03:32.079 --> 00:03:33.079
Right.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:43.389
And a lot of them care about economics more
than anything, but.

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:50.129
Yeah, no one's reaching out to you, you can't
expect them to change, I don't think.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:04:03.110
Speaker 1: Yeah, I think it's a great starting
point.

00:04:03.110 --> 00:04:21.440
It would 
be great from people that are more urban on

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:35.629
the left to spend some time in these areas
to just start understanding what's going on.

00:04:35.629 --> 00:04:54.300
I appreciate you bringing that 
point up.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:55.449
Speaker 2: Of course.

00:04:55.449 --> 00:05:01.039
Speaker 1: All right, Luke from Indiana, thank
you very much.

